<title>INDIA: TABLE-NESTLE INDIA SIX-MONTH NET STABLE.</title>
<headline>TABLE-NESTLE INDIA SIX-MONTH NET STABLE.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 29, 1997</p>
<p>		(in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit from operations    223  vs    223</p>
<p>    Net sales			 6,246  vs  5,100</p>
<p>    Other income			 42  vs     33</p>
<p>    Total expenditure	     5,632  vs  4,521</p>
<p>    Interest costs		    284  vs    261</p>
<p>    Depreciation			135  vs    118</p>
<p>    Provision for tax		  14  vs     10</p>
<p>NOTE: Nestle India Ltd, a unit of Nestle SA, said in a statement that it had commissioned its sixth plant in India at Bicholim in the western state of Goa. It said depreciation rose due to the capitalisation of projects. An interim dividend of 2.50 rupees per share was paid in June, it said.</p>
<p>-- New Delhi Newsroom (91) 11-301-2024; Fax (91) 11-301-4043</p>
